{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-minimal-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.47: the `rates-minimal` run computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE through `moves-onroad.esm` at RATES SCALE -- `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`, MOVES's MESOSCALE_LOOKUP, DEFAULT domain. It is `scale-rates` under another name -- only the description and the output database differ -- and the two runs' RatePerDistance agree in 1999 of 2000 cells; the one that differs is MOVES's own run-to-run noise (PLAN.md §7.3.47).\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. Every other RunSpec in this tree is at inventory scale and its oracle is MOVESOutput. This one's MOVESOutput is EMPTY -- MOVES deletes it after the rates post-processor has read it -- and its oracle is `RatePerDistance`: one row per (cohort, speed bin) with the rate per MILE at that bin, a link per bin (`linkID = (zoneID*10 + roadTypeID)*100 + avgSpeedBinID`), and the hour's temperature and humidity. The selections are `expand-day`'s weekday, so the same rates the inventory weights by `avgSpeedDistribution` are here one bin at a time, normalized by the cohort's own source-bin fractions instead of weighted by them (BaseRateGenerator step 008).\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `n_ratesScale` = 1 is the RunSpec's `<modelscale>`, which no table states; it sizes the speed-bin axis of the rate relation to the 16 discovered bins. `n_outputRate` = 125 is the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs, checked by `rateSurvivorCount` as everywhere else.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "rates-minimal"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-minimal/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-minimal/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecmonth"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, monthID 8 -- the XML's `<month key=\"7\"/>` is a 0-based index (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspechour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-minimal/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspechour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, hourID 7 -- `<beginhour key=\"6\"/>`, likewise an index. 59.5 degF and 90.4 % relative humidity, the two values every RatePerDistance row carries.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_aggregationhour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-minimal/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_aggregationhour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The hours the run aggregates over. It does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspechour` itself and the same file.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-minimal/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecday.parquet"
